# Combat Analysis off: a Dragoon captures a Wagon Train, then an Artillery attacking in the open loses
# to a lone Colonist and is damaged.
# Start: turns_war_combat's start (France, Spring 1600, turn 108, at war with England; French units
# sentried), fixture: head.game_options.combat_analysis off; English Wagon Train #98 moved to (44,23)
# (NW of Quebec), English Colonist #85 moved to (46,25) (SE of Quebec, open grassland, no orders);
# Quebec's Artillery #139 woken (no orders, full moves); re-saved once.
# Rolls come from the saved LCG, so the outcomes are fixed.
key KP_7                 # veteran Dragoon #131 attacks the Wagon Train: no analysis dialog
wait 3
key Return               # "{English} wagon train CAPTURED by the {French}!" (@WAGONCAPTURE): wagon flips to France, joins Quebec's tile
wait 3
                         #  Artillery #139 selected next (no outcome popup: #1464/#1465)
key KP_3                 # Artillery attacks the Colonist: open-field >>2 on the gun (docs/combat.md peels), loses
wait 3
key Return               # "French Artillery {damaged}. Further damage will destroy it." (@ARTILLERY; damaged bit set, moves spent)
wait 3
                         #  nothing left to move (no outcome popup: #1464/#1465)
shot
